request.description:
SFeed native_batch market-data feed (SDK: client.create_websocket()). In Postman: create a NEW 'WebSocket Request' (not this stub) to this URL.

After connect, send the auth frame (JSON):
{"user":"<ucc>","auth":"<edit_sid>","format":"native_batch","source":"NEOTRADEAPI","platform":"Web","version":"1.2.3","sdk_version":2,"sdk_date":"<iso-timestamp>","conn_req_time":<epoch_ms>,"sessionValidation":false}

Then a subscribe frame, e.g.:

Subscribe LTP:
{"event":"subscribeScrips","inputtoken":"nse_cm|11536","ack_symbol":true}

Subscribe indices:
{"event":"subscribeIndices","inputtoken":"nse_cm|Nifty 50","ack_symbol":true}

Unsubscribe:
{"event":"unsubscribeScrips","inputtoken":"nse_cm|11536"}

Limitation: Postman shows text frames but does not decode the binary market-data packets or automate the auth handshake. Use the SDK (create_websocket) for real data, which also withholds delivery of ticks that arrive before the subscribe acknowledgement (message_code 1109) -- keeping only the latest tick per instrument in memory -- and delivers them enriched with trading_symbol as soon as the acknowledgement lands, instead of delivering an unresolved trading_symbol early.
